@prefix ldh:    <https://w3id.org/atomgraph/linkeddatahub#> .
@prefix rdf:    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix dh:     <https://www.w3.org/ns/ldt/document-hierarchy#> .
@prefix dct:    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
   
<> a dh:Item ;
    dct:title "Change layout" ;
    dct:description "How to customize the layout of an application and the UI of the resources" ;
    rdf:_1 <#content> .
    
<#content> a ldh:XHTML ;
    rdf:value """<div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
    <p class="lead">How to customize the layout of an application and the UI of the resources</p>
    <p>LinkedDataHub's user interface is simply a rendering of the underlying Linked Data resource descriptions, which are exposed via the <a href="../../reference/http-api/" target="_blank">HTTP API</a>.</p>
    <p>LinkedDataHub provides <a href="../../reference/stylesheets/" target="_blank">XSLT stylesheets</a> that render a default UI layout. When building an application you might want to render a custom
        layout however. The recommended way of doing that is to create a new stylesheet which imports the system stylesheet and only override specific templates, while reusing the rest of the layout.</p>
    <div>
        <h2 id="create-stylesheet">Create a stylesheet</h2>
        <p>First we need to create a new XSLT 3.0 stylesheet and use <code>&lt;xsl:import&gt;</code> to import the system stylesheet <a href="https://github.com/AtomGraph/LinkedDataHub/blob/master/src/main/webapp/static/com/atomgraph/linkeddatahub/xsl/bootstrap/2.3.2/layout.xsl" target="_blank"><samp>static/com/atomgraph/linkeddatahub/xsl/bootstrap/2.3.2/layout.xsl</samp></a>:</p>
        <pre>&lt;?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?&gt;
&lt;xsl:stylesheet version="3.0"
xmlns:xsl="http://www.w3.org/1999/XSL/Transform"
xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
xmlns:foaf="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/"
xmlns:schema="https://schema.org/"
xmlns:bs2="http://graphity.org/xsl/bootstrap/2.3.2"
xmlns:ac="https://w3id.org/atomgraph/client#"
exclude-result-prefixes="#all"&gt;

    &lt;xsl:import href="https://localhost:4443/static/com/atomgraph/linkeddatahub/xsl/bootstrap/2.3.2/layout.xsl"/&gt;

    &lt;!-- overriding templates go here --&gt;

&lt;/xsl:stylesheet&gt;</pre>
        <p>(Imports under the application's <samp>/static/</samp> path resolve to local webapp files, so no HTTP round-trip is made.)</p>
    </div>
    <div>
        <h2 id="configure-dataspace">Configure the dataspace</h2>
        <div>
            <p>First, either <a href="../upload-file/" target="_blank">upload the XSLT file</a> or mount it using Docker and <samp>docker-compose.override.yml</samp>:</p>
            <pre>services:
  linkeddatahub:
    volumes:
      - ./files/northwind.xsl:/usr/local/tomcat/webapps/ROOT/static/com/atomgraph/linkeddatahub/northwind/xsl/layout.xsl:ro</pre>
            <p>Then change the value of <code>ac:stylesheet</code> on the dataspace with base URI <code>https://localhost:4443/</code> to the URL of the stylesheet. The value has to be an absolute URL on the application's own origin:</p>
            <pre>&lt;urn:linkeddatahub:apps/end-user&gt; a lapp:Application ;
    ...
    ac:stylesheet &lt;https://localhost:4443/static/com/atomgraph/linkeddatahub/northwind/xsl/layout.xsl&gt; ;
    ...</pre>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div>
        <h2 id="default-layout">Default layout</h2>
        <p>The examples below run on a Northwind <a href="https://northwind-traders.demo.linkeddatahub.com/orders/10248/" target="_blank">order document</a>:
            its graph holds the order (the document's topic) and the order's line items, each carrying its own <code>schema:price</code> line total.</p>
        <p>At this point, the default layout renders the order and each line item as a plain resource description.</p>
        <!-- screenshot: a Northwind order document in the default layout, order and line items as generic resource descriptions -->
    </div>
    <div>
        <h2 id="augment-output">Augment output</h2>
        <p>Keep the default output using <code>&lt;xsl:apply-imports&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;xsl:next-match&gt;</code> and add new output before/after it.
            Here the order's rendering gains a computed total, summed over the line items in the graph:</p>
        <pre><code>&lt;xsl:template match="*[foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf/@rdf:resource = $ac:uri][rdf:type/@rdf:resource = 'https://schema.org/Order'][key('resources', schema:orderedItem/@rdf:resource)]" priority="1"&gt;
    &lt;xsl:next-match/&gt;

    &lt;h3&gt;Order total&lt;/h3&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;
        &lt;xsl:value-of select="format-number(sum(key('resources', schema:orderedItem/@rdf:resource)/schema:price), '#,##0.00')"/&gt;
        &lt;xsl:text&gt; USD&lt;/xsl:text&gt;
    &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/xsl:template&gt;</code></pre>
        <p>The match pattern will match the resource descriptions that:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>are the primary topic of the requested document (i.e. its order) <em>and</em> are typed <code>schema:Order</code> <em>and</em> have line item(s) present in the RDF graph</li>
        </ul>
        <p>With the overriding template, the order page shows the computed total after the order's default description.</p>
        <!-- screenshot: the augmented order page with the Order total heading and sum under the order description -->
    </div>
    <div>
        <h2 id="override-output">Override output</h2>
        <p>To completely change the layout without keeping the default one, use the same logic as for <a href="#augment-output">augmenting</a> it, but do not call <code>&lt;xsl:apply-imports&gt;</code>/<code>&lt;xsl:next-match&gt;</code>.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
        <h2 id="suppress-output">Suppress output</h2>
        <p>Having summed the line items into a total, we may no longer want each line item rendered as its own resource description, nor the raw
            <code>schema:orderedItem</code> rows in the order's property list.</p>
        <p>You can specify an empty template at any level (graph/property/resource) to disable output of that layout mode. This suppresses the line item resources:</p>
        <pre><code>&lt;xsl:template match="*[@rdf:about = key('resources', key('resources', $ac:uri)/foaf:primaryTopic/@rdf:resource)/schema:orderedItem/@rdf:resource]"/&gt;</code></pre>
        <p>The match pattern will match the resource descriptions that:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>are line items of the primary topic of the current document</li>
        </ul>
        <p>and this suppresses the property rows:</p>
        <pre>&lt;xsl:template match="*[foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf/@rdf:resource = $ac:uri]/schema:orderedItem" mode="bs2:PropertyList"/&gt;</pre>
        <p>The match pattern will match the resource properties that:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>are <code>schema:orderedItem</code> properties of a resource that is the primary topic of the current document</li>
        </ul>
        <p>With the suppressing templates, the order page shows the order, its total, and nothing else twice.</p>
        <!-- screenshot: the order page after suppression - order description and total only, line items hidden -->
    </div>
</div>"""^^rdf:XMLLiteral .
